tialPrices\\|SeedData\\|Seed\" src/DcaShop.Pricing src/DcaShop.Infrastructure | grep \"\\.cs$\"","description":"Find shipping costs and price seeds"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_013MTQFkVwHkXhHVCxupHNxW","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-knowledge-catalog/bundle && grep -ril \"translation site\\|one translation\\|external system\" . | head -15","description":"Search knowledge catalog for relevant nodes"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KfjNLiWNZP928Y79LARjg3","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-knowledge-catalog/bundle && cat pitfall/mocking-the-port-of-the-changed-adapter.md recipe/test-a-scenario-integrated.md rule/contextmap/dca-map-008.md | head -150","description":"Read relevant catalog nodes"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":33,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the plan to `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/plan.md`. I didn't run the plan gate, so that check is still to do.\n\n**What the story changes (Checkout context):**\n- The payment step can now tell two failures apart: the provider refused the payment, or the provider is unavailable. The use case turns them into the two failure types that already exist.\n- A new REST adapter, `RestPaymentProvider`, calls `POST /payments` with the amount and currency and gives up after 2 seconds. It sits in `Adapter/Outgoing/Payment`, and the provider's own data types stay inside it.\n- The adapter is used only when `Checkout:PaymentProvider:BaseUrl` is set. Without it the stand-in stays, so all existing tests keep paying through `\"mock\"` unchanged.\n- The checkout page controller shows the two customer texts from the story in the payment page's existing error box.\n- The description of the external provider on `CheckoutContext` gets updated, which regenerates `docs/architecture/context-map.md`.\n\n**Test levels:**\n- **Happy path:** a browser test with a WireMock.Net stub standing in for the provider.\n- **Refusal and slow provider:** integration tests that send `POST /checkout/payment` to the app running in the test, with WireMock.Net as the provider.\n\nNo existing test contradicts the story, so there's no `## Changed tests` section and no decision for you to answer. The designed and generated context maps agree, and nothing needs a new page or endpoint.\n\n**Assumptions you should check** (listed in the plan):\n- **Field names:** `project/tech.md` doesn't name the JSON fields. I assumed the request is `{amount, currency}` and a `201` answer carries `{reference}`.\n- **Other answers:** any answer other than `201` or `402` counts as \"unavailable\".\n- **Missing endpoints:** the provider contract has no availability, confirm or cancel endpoint. The adapter says it is always available, confirms without calling the provider, and reports cancellation as failed; the use case already logs that as a warning.\n- **Provider name:** when the address is configured, the REST provider replaces the stand-in. Its id (`provider`) and display name (\"Payment provider\") are my guesses.\n- **Running the browser test:** it only runs when the shop was started pointing at the test's stub. It reads the address from an environment variable I proposed, `E2E_PAYMENT_PROVIDER_URL`, the same way `EmbeddedModeFact` works.\n- **Outside this story:** the Java sample needs the same change, and the browser test needs a matching scenario in the shared specification's `scenarios.md`. Both are yours to decide.","ttft_ms":2915,"type":"result","duration_ms":229033,"uuid":"6c2012bc-76b2-4bb1-8fe0-732337a12b5b","ttft_stream_ms":1715,"time_to_request_ms":87,"first_content_frame_ms":1715,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
